    {
      "id": "sol.hmmt-feb-algebra-2001-p4.hmmt",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "\\(7,999,999,999=8 \\cdot 10^{9}-1=2000^{3}-1=(2000-1)\\left(2000^{2}+2000+1\\right)\\), so \\(\\left(2000^{2}+2000+1\\right)=4,002,001\\) is its largest prime factor.",
